e first and the routing set is read off the built subparser instead of maintained beside it, making a routed-but-unregistered command unrepresentable; the derived set differs from the old list by exactly these seven and all 42 known commands now dispatch. PLUGIN PEPPER MANAGEMENT CLI (gitlab#193): the remote-pepper plugin's operations had working business logic but no argparse surface, so the desktop GUI's pepper controls emitted argv (plugin pepper list/test/setup-totp/verify-totp/configure-deadman) that exited 2 with 'invalid choice' and the GUI swallowed the failure — a new `plugin pepper` subcommand tree wires all of them: list (stored peppers as JSON), test (ad-hoc mTLS connectivity probe from --url/--client-cert/--client-key/--ca-cert), setup-totp/verify-totp (TOTP 2FA enrolment) and configure-deadman (the pepper dead-man's switch); the only secret payloads — the TOTP shared secret and the one-time backup codes — are emitted on stdout ONLY (never stderr, which the GUI persists to its debug log) and registered with the audit-log redactor, mirroring generate-password --json, and --code is added to the --debug argv-redaction set; configure-deadman --interval/--grace-period take whole days and are refused below 1, because the switch auto-wipes every pepper on a missed check-in so a zero/negative deadline must never be armable with an already-past auto-wipe, and the destructive panic operation is deliberately not exposed. PLUGIN INTEGRITY VERIFICATION CLI (gitlab#194): the remote file-integrity plugin (test/stats/verify) likewise had no CLI surface, so the GUI's integrity controls could not reach it — a new `plugin integrity` subcommand tree wires test (mTLS probe), stats (verification statistics as JSON) and verify --file-id --metadata-hash, whose verify uses a deliberately FOUR-outcome contract so a file the service never registered or a service that cannot be reached can NEVER be reported as a tamper alarm (the exact bug the removed GUI batch path had, collapsin